{"id": "en_hurricane_p2", "total": 74.67, "segments": [{"text": "Part two. Rising water floods the hallway while live power lines spark downstairs.", "start": 0.0, "end": 4.58}, {"text": "Jake climbs onto high furniture inside his interior room to stay above water.", "start": 5.08, "end": 8.36}, {"text": "One. Do not walk or drive through flood water after a storm hits.", "start": 9.02, "end": 12.7}, {"text": "Hidden electrical currents from downed power lines make standing flood water extremely dangerous.", "start": 13.34, "end": 17.36}, {"text": "Water surge causes most hurricane deaths, so Jake remains inside his concrete sanctuary.", "start": 17.94, "end": 21.98}, {"text": "He sits away from windows inside interior rooms while wind slams the building.", "start": 22.6, "end": 25.96}, {"text": "Two. Run from water, hide from wind inside a sturdy reinforced hotel building.", "start": 26.6, "end": 31.0}, {"text": "High above ground, thick concrete walls protect him as violent ocean swells crash.", "start": 31.44, "end": 35.28}, {"text": "After long hours, the storm surge recedes and ocean waters pull back out.", "start": 35.94, "end": 39.2}, {"text": "Three. Watch for downed power lines when exiting your shelter after severe storms.", "start": 39.94, "end": 43.7}, {"text": "Jake begins to walk to shelter exit doors, stepping carefully around wet areas.", "start": 44.52, "end": 47.92}, {"text": "He notices broken power lines hanging near deep water puddles on the ground.", "start": 48.4, "end": 51.28}, {"text": "Rescue teams establish safe paths past dangerous electrical hazard zones for all survivors.", "start": 52.08, "end": 55.92}, {"text": "Jake will walk to shelter evacuation vehicles parked on elevated dry ground nearby.", "start": 56.74, "end": 59.94}, {"text": "He must enter shelter transport buses away from hazardous standing flood water outdoors.", "start": 60.42, "end": 64.04}, {"text": "Always run from water and hide from wind during severe hurricane stor